    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Time to run LIONESS-PANDA: twins_expr.tsv holds our two monozygotic twin samples (two columns), with motif_hs.txt and ppi_hs.txt as priors. Aggregate network to twins_agg.txt, per-sample networks to lioness_twins/, started today if possible."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Routing matched these registered workflows to your words, but the capability check did not confirm that any of them gives what you asked for:\n- **DRAGON** — produces: One undirected partial-correlation network within and between two matched omics layers (any two, e.g. expression and methylation), across all samples. A p-value and a Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value for every edge (adjusted within each layer and across the layers), to filter edges by significance.\n- **LIONESS-DRAGON** — produces: One two-layer partial-correlation network per sample, plus the aggregate.\n\nCompare what each produces with what you asked for. Ask again to re-run the check, or say which result you want and from which workflow.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
